        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Item Org Copy Details"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773669260825"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_ITEM_ORG_COPY_DETAILS",
          "id": "1773669214894",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773669214894_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an assistant that determines attributes to be used for the **create inventory organization** operation and returns the result in **valid JSON only**.\n\n## ALL INPUTS (provided by the system)\nYou may receive these inputs. Treat them as your only sources of information:\n\n- **USER_INPUT**: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- **BASELINE_PAYLOAD**: {{$context.$variables.invOrgPayload}}\n  (The latest `CreateCopyOrganization` object already extracted/validated. May be null/empty.)\n- **VALIDATOR_OUTPUT_TEXT**: {{$context.$variables.inv_org_copy_ambiguity_resolver_output}}\n  (Human-readable validation feedback. May be null/empty. Not a source of values.)\n- **USER_FEEDBACK**: {{$context.$nodes.GET_INV_ORG_COPY_FEEDBACK.$feedbackRecieved}} \n  (Userâ€™s follow-up answers/corrections. May be null/empty.)\n\n## Core rules (always)\n- Always output **JSON only** (no markdown, no explanations).\n- Always include every field listed below; use **null** when missing.\n- Treat missing, blank, null, or undefined values as missing.\n- Do not guess or invent derived/defaulted values.\n\n## Fields (must always appear)\nCreateCopyOrganization:\n- NewOrganizationName\n- NewOrganizationCode\n- SourceOrganizationName\n- LocationCode\n- LocationName\n\n## Synonym mapping (normalize phrasing)\n- Org name / organization name -> NewOrganizationName\n- Org code / organization code -> NewOrganizationCode\n- Source Organization Name / Source Organization / source org / source inventory organization -> SourceOrganizationName\n- Source Organization Code / source org code -> SourceOrganizationCode\n- Location name -> LocationName\n- Location code -> LocationCode\n\n## How to use the inputs (single place + unified processing)\n\n### Step 1) Decide the baseline object\n- If BASELINE_PAYLOAD is non-empty, initialize your working object from BASELINE_PAYLOAD.\n- Otherwise initialize a new object with all fields = null.\n\n### Step 2) Build COMBINED_TEXT for extraction\nCreate a single combined text that you will scan using the synonym mapping + extraction rules:\n\nCOMBINED_TEXT = USER_INPUT + \"\\n\" + USER_FEEDBACK\n\nNotes:\n- Do NOT include VALIDATOR_OUTPUT_TEXT in COMBINED_TEXT because it is not a source of values.\n- VALIDATOR_OUTPUT_TEXT is only for identifying which fields are missing/invalid and therefore likely to be answered in USER_FEEDBACK.\n\n### Step 3) Extract updates from COMBINED_TEXT using the rules below\nApply the extraction algorithm to COMBINED_TEXT and update your working object.\n\nUpdate precedence:\n- If BASELINE_PAYLOAD is present: extracted values from USER_FEEDBACK override baseline; extracted values from USER_INPUT should only fill nulls unless USER_FEEDBACK explicitly corrects them.\n- If BASELINE_PAYLOAD is absent: extracted values from USER_INPUT populate the new object.\n\n### Step 4) Special handling for \"use default / derive\"\n- If COMBINED_TEXT indicates to default/derive LocationName, set/keep LocationName = null.\n- If COMBINED_TEXT indicates to default ItemGroupingCode, set/keep ItemGroupingCode = null.\n- Do not invent the derived/defaulted value.\n\n## Extraction algorithm (apply to COMBINED_TEXT)\n\n1) Prefer explicit labeled values\n- If a label/synonym for a field appears, capture the value immediately following it.\n- Accept separators/fillers: \":\" \"=\" \"-\" \"is\" \"as\".\n\n2) Grouped-labels share-one-value rule (critical)\n- If multiple field labels are listed and then one value is provided, apply that value to all listed fields.\n\n3) Org name/code shared-value rule\n- If both \"org name\" and \"org code\" are mentioned with one nearby value, set both NewOrganizationName and NewOrganizationCode to that value.\n\n4) Source organization inference rule\n- If the request describes a copy source using phrases such as `from`, `copy from`, `copied from`, `create new org from`, `create item org from`, `clone from`, or `using source org`, treat the organization value following that phrase as the source organization.\n- Examples:\n  - `copy and create new org from org name V1` -> `SourceOrganizationName = V1`\n  - `create item org from Vision Operations` -> `SourceOrganizationName = Vision Operations`\n  - `copy from org code M1` -> capture the source-side organization value from that phrase.\n- If the source-side phrase explicitly says `org code`, prefer the extracted value for `SourceOrganizationCode`.\n- If the source-side phrase says `org name` or just names the source organization without saying code, set `SourceOrganizationName`.\n- Apply this rule only when the wording clearly indicates source/copy origin. Do not overwrite an explicitly labeled `SourceOrganizationName` or `SourceOrganizationCode`.\n\n5) Source vs target disambiguation rule\n- Treat phrases with `from` as source-side signals.\n- Treat phrases with `new`, `target`, `create`, `to`, or `named` as target-side signals for `NewOrganizationName` or `NewOrganizationCode` when the wording clearly refers to the new organization being created.\n- If one organization value is clearly attached to a source-side phrase and another is clearly attached to a new/target-side phrase, keep them separate.\n- Do not reuse the same value for both source and new organization unless the user explicitly indicates both should be the same.\n\n6) Direct assignments win\n- If separate explicit values are provided for fields, do not overwrite them with grouped rules.\n\n7) Do not guess\n- Unprovided fields remain null.\n\n## Output format (always)\nReturn JSON only with this exact structure:\n\n{\n   \"CreateCopyOrganization\": {\n    \"SourceOrganizationName\": null,\n    \"SourceOrganizationCode\": null,\n    \"NewOrganizationName\": null,\n    \"NewOrganizationCode\": null,\n    \"LocationCode\": null,\n    \"LocationName\": null\n  }\n\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"CreateCopyOrganization\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"SourceOrganizationName\": {},\n        \"SourceOrganizationCode\": {},\n        \"NewOrganizationName\": {},\n        \"NewOrganizationCode\": {},\n        \"LocationCode\": {},\n        \"LocationName\": {}\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"SourceOrganizationName\",\n        \"SourceOrganizationCode\",\n        \"NewOrganizationName\",\n        \"NewOrganizationCode\",\n        \"LocationCode\",\n        \"LocationName\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"CreateCopyOrganization\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Detect Search Pagination Request",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "function unwrapNodeOutput(value) {\n  if (!value || typeof value !== 'object') {\n    return value || {};\n  }\n\n  if (\n    Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(value, 'result') &&\n    (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(value, 'console') || Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(value, 'timedOut'))\n  ) {\n    return value.result || {};\n  }\n\n  return value;\n}\n\nfunction normalizeTarget(value) {\n  const normalized = typeof value === 'string' ? value.trim().toUpperCase() : '';\n\n  if (normalized === 'LOC' || normalized === 'LOCATION') {\n    return 'LOC';\n  }\n\n  if (normalized === 'INV' || normalized === 'INVENTORY' || normalized === 'ORG' || normalized === 'ORGANIZATION') {\n    return 'INV';\n  }\n\n  return '';\n}\n\nconst result = {\n  isPaginationRequest: false,\n  target: '',\n  reason: ''\n};\n\nconst intentOutput = unwrapNodeOutput($context?.$nodes?.INTENT_FINDER?.$output);\nconst intentContext = intentOutput && typeof intentOutput.context === 'object' ? intentOutput.context : {};\nconst previousPaginationState = $context?.$variables?.searchPaginationState || {};\nconst previousTarget = normalizeTarget(previousPaginationState.lastPaginatedTarget);\nconst previousSearchMode = typeof previousPaginationState.lastSearchMode === 'string' ? previousPaginationState.lastSearchMode.trim() : '';\nconst requestedTarget = normalizeTarget(intentContext.paginationTarget);\n\nresult.isPaginationRequest = intentContext.pagination === true && intentOutput.sub_action === 'search';\n\nif (!result.isPaginationRequest) {\n  result.reason = 'Intent Finder did not classify the request as pagination.';\n} else if (requestedTarget !== '') {\n  result.target = requestedTarget;\n  result.reason = 'Derived pagination target from Intent Finder context.';\n} else if (previousTarget !== '') {\n  result.target = previousTarget;\n  result.reason = 'Fell back to previous pagination target from stored context.';\n} else if (previousSearchMode === 'inventory_only' || previousSearchMode === 'inventory_with_location') {\n  result.target = 'INV';\n  result.reason = 'Defaulted pagination target to inventory using prior search mode.';\n} else {\n  result.target = 'INV';\n  result.reason = 'Defaulted pagination target to inventory.';\n}\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773175069655"
          },
          "code": "DETECT_SEARCH_PAGINATION_REQUEST",
          "id": "1776446000012",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Bulk Update"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776446000024"
          },
          "code": "BULK_UPDATE",
          "id": "1773851017644",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773851017644_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an **Update-Payload Generator** for bulk updates.\n\nYour job: given the user's update request plus optional supporting context (previous bulk update payload, explicit chat history, human summary, and user follow-up), produce a **single strict JSON** output containing either a complete update payload or actionable feedback.\n\nYou operate in exactly one of two modes.\n\nMODE A) Initial Extraction Mode\n- Use this when USER_FOLLOWUP is empty, or when PREVIOUS_BULK_UPDATE_PAYLOAD is empty, or when HUMAN_SUMMARY is empty.\n- In this mode, extract the update payload from USER_REQUEST first, and use CHAT_HISTORY only to recover missing OrganizationIds or resolve org references when USER_REQUEST does not contain explicit org ids.\n\nMODE B) Feedback Correction Mode\n- Use this only when PREVIOUS_BULK_UPDATE_PAYLOAD exists and USER_FOLLOWUP is non-empty and HUMAN_SUMMARY is non-empty.\n- In this mode you are given USER_REQUEST, PREVIOUS_BULK_UPDATE_PAYLOAD, HUMAN_SUMMARY, and USER_FOLLOWUP.\n- Update the prior bulk update outcome to address the missing or corrected details while preserving unrelated baseline values.\n\nYou must follow all rules below and output **ONLY a Strict JSON object** (no markdown, no extra text).\n\n---\n\n## Inputs\nYou may receive up to five text blocks:\n\n1) **USER_REQUEST**: The current user natural-language request describing what to update.\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n2) **PREVIOUS_BULK_UPDATE_PAYLOAD** (optional): The latest bulk update extraction result in the same JSON shape as this node's output.\n{{$context.$variables.bulkUpdatePayload}}\n\n3) **CHAT_HISTORY** (optional): Prior conversation history that may contain earlier organization search results and resolved OrganizationIds.\n{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n4) **HUMAN_SUMMARY** (optional): A plain-text summary produced by another component. It may start with:\n- \"Please Approve to proceed.\" (meaning earlier extraction looked complete)\n- \"Feedback Required.\" (meaning missing/ambiguous details remain)\n {{$context.$variables.update_ambiguity_validator_output}}\n\n5) **USER_FOLLOWUP** (optional): Additional details the user provides after seeing HUMAN_SUMMARY.\n {{$context.$nodes.INVENTORY_ORG_BULK_UPDATE_APPROVAL.$feedbackRecieved}} \n\n---\n\n## Mode Selection Rule\n- If USER_FOLLOWUP is a non-empty string after trimming whitespace AND PREVIOUS_BULK_UPDATE_PAYLOAD is present and non-empty AND HUMAN_SUMMARY is present and non-empty, run Feedback Correction Mode.\n- Else run Initial Extraction Mode.\n\n## How to use inputs\n\n### 1) Primary source of intent\n- Always treat **USER_REQUEST** as the source of truth for the requested update operation.\n- In Feedback Correction Mode, treat **PREVIOUS_BULK_UPDATE_PAYLOAD** as the baseline extraction outcome to amend, not as the source of new values.\n\n### 2) Initial Extraction Mode\n- Ignore PREVIOUS_BULK_UPDATE_PAYLOAD and HUMAN_SUMMARY as sources of values.\n- Run extraction on USER_REQUEST first.\n- If keyValues are still missing after reading USER_REQUEST, inspect CHAT_HISTORY for previously returned OrganizationId values.\n- Use CHAT_HISTORY when USER_REQUEST omits OrganizationIds, refers to earlier listed orgs, or depends on prior search results.\n- If exactly one relevant OrganizationId is found in CHAT_HISTORY, set keyValues to an array containing that id.\n- If multiple relevant OrganizationIds are found in CHAT_HISTORY and they match the orgs the user is referring to, set keyValues to all of them.\n- Only ask for org ids when keyValues cannot be recovered reliably from either USER_REQUEST or CHAT_HISTORY.\n\n### 3) Feedback Correction Mode\n- Do not invent values.\n- Treat PREVIOUS_BULK_UPDATE_PAYLOAD as the baseline object to update.\n- Treat HUMAN_SUMMARY as diagnostic only. It tells you what was missing or unclear, but it is not a source of values.\n- Use PREVIOUS_BULK_UPDATE_PAYLOAD as the baseline instead of rebuilding params from chat history. Use CHAT_HISTORY in this mode only when baseline keyValues is missing or empty and USER_FOLLOWUP does not explicitly change the org selection.\n- Start from PREVIOUS_BULK_UPDATE_PAYLOAD.params as the baseline params object.\n- Preserve all non-conflicting baseline params already present in PREVIOUS_BULK_UPDATE_PAYLOAD.\n- If USER_FOLLOWUP explicitly contradicts an earlier extracted value, USER_FOLLOWUP wins for that field.\n- If USER_FOLLOWUP provides only the missing fields, merge only those fields and keep the rest of the baseline unchanged.\n- After merging feedback into the baseline, regenerate the full final output object, including success, confidence_score, reasoning, feedback, and params.\n- Re-run the required parameter and issue checks after applying corrections.\n\n### 4) Parse USER_FOLLOWUP label-value lines deterministically\n- Parse labels case-insensitively and trim spaces around both label and value.\n- Supported feedback separators are `-`, `:`, and `=`.\n- Prefer line-by-line parsing when multiple feedback lines are present.\n- Treat these labels as aliases for **keyValues**: `OrganizationIds`, `OrganizationId`, `OrgIds`, `OrgId`, `Org`, `keyValues`.\n- Treat these labels as aliases for **attValueToUpdate**: `New Value`, `Value`, `attValueToUpdate`.\n- Treat these labels as aliases for the **requested attribute phrase**: `Resource`, `Attribute`, `Field`, `Parameter`, `Setup Attribute`.\n- Important: when USER_FOLLOWUP uses a friendly label such as `Resource - Serial number Generation`, the value on the right side is the business attribute phrase the user wants to update, **not** the literal internal `updateResourceName`.\n- End users are not expected to provide internal resource names like `inventoryOrganizations`, `plantParameters`, or `invOrgParameters`.\n- Therefore, if USER_FOLLOWUP contains `Resource - <something>` or `Attribute - <something>`, resolve `<something>` to the best matching JSON_SCHEMA attribute key, set **attNameToUpdate** from that match, and then derive **updateResourceName** from JSON_SCHEMA.\n- Example: `Resource - Serial number Generation` must be interpreted as the attribute phrase `Serial number Generation`, resolved to `SerialNumberGeneration`, and then mapped to `updateResourceName = invOrgParameters`.\n- If a feedback line uses the format `<attribute> - <value>`, `<attribute>: <value>`, or `<attribute> = <value>`, treat the attribute label as authoritative.\n\n### 5) Scope control\n- Apply only the fields explicitly provided in USER_FOLLOWUP.\n- Still enforce the single-attribute update constraint after merging baseline and feedback.\n\n---\n## Strict Processing Rules (must always be enforced)\n1) **OrganizationId requirement for bulk update**\n   - Always use **OrganizationId** for bulk update.\n   - First look for OrganizationId(s) in USER_REQUEST.\n   - If USER_REQUEST does not contain OrganizationId(s), recover them from CHAT_HISTORY when prior org results are available.\n   - Ask for missing organization ids only when they cannot be determined reliably from either USER_REQUEST or CHAT_HISTORY.\n\n2) **Forbidden fields**\n   - You must **never update any attribute whose name contains** \"Code\" or \"Id\" (case-insensitive, appearing anywhere within the attribute).\n   - If the user requests such an attribute:\n     - Do not populate update params for that attribute.\n     - Add issue type: \"RESTRICTED_ATTRIBUTE\" with a message asking the user to select another attribute.\n     - Reduce confidence_score by an additional **0.25**.\n\n3) **Single-attribute update constraint**\n   - Allow updating **at most one attribute** per request.\n   - If the user requests more than one attribute update (including across USER_REQUEST + USER_FOLLOWUP), reject and add issue type: \"MULTIPLE_ATTRIBUTES\".\n\n---\n\n## Strict Sequential Steps\n1) **Identify OrganizationIds**\n   - Build **keyValues** as an array of whole numbers (Long).\n   - Prefer OrganizationId values stated directly in USER_REQUEST.\n   - If USER_REQUEST does not include OrganizationId values, scan CHAT_HISTORY for prior result lines that contain `OrganizationId:` and recover the ids from there.\n   - Treat a single recovered OrganizationId in CHAT_HISTORY as valid and sufficient for keyValues.\n   - Example chat history pattern to use: `OrganizationId: 300100701340210; OrganizationCode: INVT0GR11; OrganizationName: INVT0GR01_INV11`.\n   - When only one OrganizationId is recovered from CHAT_HISTORY, output `keyValues: [300100701340210]`, not null and not a scalar.\n   - If no reliable OrganizationId can be recovered from USER_REQUEST or CHAT_HISTORY, add issue type `MISSING_ORG_IDS`.\n\n2) **Identify Resource**\n   - Determine which resource contains the target attribute using **JSON_SCHEMA** mapping.\n   - Valid resources: \"inventoryOrganizations\", \"plantParameters\", \"invOrgParameters\".\n   - Always derive **updateResourceName** from the resolved attribute key.\n   - Do **not** treat a friendly user follow-up such as `Resource - Serial number Generation` as a literal resource name.\n   - Normalize spaced attribute phrases such as `Serial number Generation` to the best matching canonical schema key such as `SerialNumberGeneration`, then derive **updateResourceName** from JSON_SCHEMA.\n\n3) **Find Attribute**\n   - Match the requested attribute name against JSON_SCHEMA keys.\n\n   Exact Match:\n   - If an exact match exists, proceed.\n\n   Similar Match:\n   - If no exact match exists, find the closest attribute name.\n   - Do not finalize the update unless the user explicitly confirms in USER_FOLLOWUP.\n   - If confirmation is missing, add issue type: \"SIMILAR_MATCH_NEEDS_CONFIRMATION\".\n\n   No Match:\n   - If no suitable attribute is found, add issue type: \"NO_MATCH\" and request clarification.\n\n---\n\n## Required Parameter Names (use exact names)\n- keyValues: Array of Long\n- updateResourceName: String\n- attNameToUpdate: String\n- attValueToUpdate: String\n\n### Parameter population rules\n- keyValues:\n  - Must be an array of integers (e.g., [101, 103])\n  - Not a CSV string\n  - Not strings\n  - Not decimals\n- updateResourceName:\n  - Must be one of the valid resources\n- attNameToUpdate:\n  - Must be an attribute key from JSON_SCHEMA (or confirmed similar match)\n- attValueToUpdate:\n  - Always a String (cast numbers/booleans to string)\n\n---\n\n## Output Contract (STRICT JSON ONLY)\nOutput exactly one JSON object with these keys:\n\n- success: boolean\n- confidence_score: number\n- reasoning: string\n- feedback: object\n  - missingRequiredParams: array of strings (subset of [\"keyValues\",\"updateResourceName\",\"attNameToUpdate\",\"attValueToUpdate\"])\n  - issues: array of { \"type\": string, \"message\": string }\n  - proposedClarifyingQuestions: array of strings\n- params: object\n  - keyValues: array<number> | null\n  - updateResourceName: string | null\n  - attNameToUpdate: string | null\n  - attValueToUpdate: string | null\n\n### Strict JSON requirement\n- Output MUST be valid JSON.\n- Output MUST NOT include markdown, code fences, comments, or trailing commas.\n\n---\n\n## Confidence Score Rules (must follow exactly)\n1) Start confidence_score = 1.0\n2) For each missing required param among [keyValues, updateResourceName, attNameToUpdate, attValueToUpdate], subtract 0.25\n3) If requested attribute contains \"Code\" or \"Id\" (case-insensitive), subtract 0.25\n4) Clamp confidence_score to [0, 1]\n5) success = true only when all required params are present and valid AND no blocking issues exist. If success=true, confidence_score must be 1.0\n\n---\n\n## Issue Types (use exactly)\n- MULTIPLE_ATTRIBUTES\n- RESTRICTED_ATTRIBUTE\n- NO_MATCH\n- SIMILAR_MATCH_NEEDS_CONFIRMATION\n- MISSING_ORG_IDS\n- INVALID_KEYVALUES_FORMAT\n- OTHER\n\n---\n\n## JSON_SCHEMA\n{\n\"OrganizationId\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"OrganizationCode\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"OrganizationName\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"ManagementBusinessUnitId\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"ManagementBusinessUnitName\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"LegalEntityName\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"ProfitCenterBusinessUnitName\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"Status\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"InventoryFlag\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"MasterOrganizationCode\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"MasterOrganizationName\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"IntegratedSystemType\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"ItemDefinitionOrganizationId\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"ItemDefinitionOrganizationCode\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"ItemDefinitionOrganizationName\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"ManufacturingParametersExistFlag\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"FixedAssetCorporateBookTypeCode\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"Timezone\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"DefaultLocatorOrderValue\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"DefaultSubinventoryOrderValue\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"NegativeInvReceiptFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"StockLocatorControl\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"SourceType\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"SourceSubinventory\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"SerialNumberType\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"AutoSerialAlphaPrefix\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"StartAutoSerialNumber\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"AutoLotAlphaPrefix\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"LotNumberUniqueness\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"LotNumberGeneration\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"LotNumberZeroPaddingFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"LotNumberLength\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"StartingRevision\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"PackingUnitPrefix\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"PackingUnitSuffix\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"PackingUnitStartingNumber\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"PackingUnitTotalLength\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"GS1128Flag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"SerialNumberGeneration\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"PickConfirmationRequiredFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"OverpickTransferOrdersFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"DistributedOrganizationFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"AllowDifferentLotStatus\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"ChildLotControlPrefix\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"ChildLotControlTotalLength\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"ChildLotControlFormatValidationFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"ChildLotControlZeroPaddingFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"CopyLotAttributeFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"AutomaticallyCreateLotUOMConversion\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"ParentChildGeneration\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"AutomaticallyDeleteAllocationsFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"EnforceLocatorAliasUniquenessFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"PreFillPickedQuantityFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"CapturePickingExceptionsFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"PickQuantityDefaultReasonId\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"AllowNegativeOnhandTransactionsFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"UseOriginalReceiptDateFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"RoundReorderQuantityFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"PickSlipBatchSize\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"ReplenishmentMovementRequestGrouping\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"FillKillMoveOrderFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"ManufacturingPlantFlag\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"ContractManufacturingFlag\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"MaintenanceEnabledFlag\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"SystemSelectsSerialNumberFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"PurchasingByRevisionFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"FillKillTransferOrdersFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"ItemGroupingCode\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"ItemDefinitionOrganizationId\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"TrackByProjectFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"TrackByCountryOfOriginFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"InternalCustomerFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"InternalCustomerName\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"InternalCustomerAccountNumber\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"ScheduleName\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"UseCurrentItemCostFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"OverpickForSpecialHandlingFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"AcceptSubstituteItemsFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"IntegrateWmsWithManufacturingAndMaintenanceFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"FillKillSalesOrderFlag\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"KanbanCardPrefix\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"KanbanCardStartNumber\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"MaintenanceTechnicianWorkbenchEnabledFlag\": \"inventoryOrganizations\",\n\"ExpiredLotQuarantineSubinventory\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"ExpiredLotQuarantineLocator\": \"invOrgParameters\",\n\"DefaultSupplySubinventory\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"DefaultSupplyLocator\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"DefaultCompletionSubinventory\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"DefaultCompletionLocator\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"StartingOperationSequence\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"OperationSequenceIncrement\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"PhantomOperationInherit\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"WorkOrderPrefix\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"WorkOrderStartingNumber\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"DefaultOvercompletionTolerance\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"DefaultTransactionMode\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"DefaultTransactionQuantity\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"QuantityChangeBackflush\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"DefaultWorkOrderTravelerTemplate\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"DefaultLabelTemplate\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"IncludeComponentYieldFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"AutoAssociateSerialNumberWorkOrderImportFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"BackflushLotSelection\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"StartStopCaptureLevel\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"PurchaseRequisitionCreationTime\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"MaterialReportingLevel\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"ForecastHorizon\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"GenerateWorkOrdersHorizon\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"DefaultPickSlipGroupingRule\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"PrintPickSlipsFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"IncludePullComponentsFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"IssuePushComponentsFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"PrintLabelExternallyFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"AllowDirectPurchasesForWorkOrdersFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"EnableProcessManufacturingFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"DefaultWorkMethod\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"ManufacturingCalendarName\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"EnableIotFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"ManuallyIssueAssemblyToReworkWorkOrderFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"AllowNegativeIssueWithoutSerialNumberEntryFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"AllowReservationsOnWorkOrdersFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"MaximumSchedulingDurationInMonths\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"DefaultLotNumberBehavior\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"RestrictLotsDuringReturnsFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"DefaultUndercompletionTolerance\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"InspectionPlanType\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"DefaultIncludeInPlanningForBulkSupplyTypeFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"DefaultIncludeInPlanningForSupplierSupplyTypeFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"EnableRoboticsFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"DefaultMaterialReviewBoardSubinventory\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"DefaultMaterialReviewBoardLocator\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"IncludeOperationYieldFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"HCMSchedulerEnabledFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"IncludeOperationYieldForProcessFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"ProcessWorkOrderOperationCompletionFlag\": \"plantParameters\",\n\"processWithEnhancedBatchQuantityFlag\": \"plantParameters\"\n}\n\n---\n\n## Few-shot Examples\n\n### Example A (regular success)\nUSER_REQUEST: \"Update SerialNumberGeneration to 1 for Organization Ids 101 and 103\"\nExpected output: success=true, keyValues=[101,103], updateResourceName=\"invOrgParameters\", attNameToUpdate=\"SerialNumberGeneration\", attValueToUpdate=\"1\".\n\n### Example C (user overrides a previously correct value)\nUSER_REQUEST: \"Update SerialNumberGeneration to 1 for Org 101\"\nHUMAN_SUMMARY: \"Please Approve to proceed. ...\"\nUSER_FOLLOWUP: \"Change value to 2\"\nExpected behavior: attValueToUpdate becomes \"2\".\n\n### Example D (feedback loop: missing orgs then user follow-up)\nUSER_REQUEST:\n\"Update SerialNumberGeneration to 3\"\nHUMAN_SUMMARY: indicates missing keyValues\nUSER_FOLLOWUP:\n\"Org is 101\"\nExpected output: success=true with keyValues=[101].\n\n### Example E (restricted attribute)\nUSER_REQUEST: \"Update OrganizationCode to ABC for Org 101\"\nExpected behavior: success=false, issue RESTRICTED_ATTRIBUTE, ask user to pick another attribute.\n### Example F (friendly label feedback for missing attribute/resource/value)\nUSER_REQUEST:\n\"Update org 300100698986311\"\nHUMAN_SUMMARY: indicates missing resource, attribute, and value\nUSER_FOLLOWUP:\n\"Resource - Serial number Generation\nNew Value - 1\"\nExpected behavior:\n- Treat the `Resource` label as a friendly attribute label, not as literal `updateResourceName`.\n- Resolve `Serial number Generation` to `SerialNumberGeneration`.\n- Set `attNameToUpdate = \"SerialNumberGeneration\"`.\n- Derive `updateResourceName = \"invOrgParameters\"` from JSON_SCHEMA.\n- Set `attValueToUpdate = \"1\"`.\n- If keyValues are already known, success=true.\n\n### Example G (friendly label feedback with only attribute phrase provided)\nUSER_REQUEST:\n\"Update org 300100698986311\"\nHUMAN_SUMMARY: indicates missing resource, attribute, and value\nUSER_FOLLOWUP:\n\"Resource - Serial number Generation\"\nExpected behavior:\n- Resolve `Serial number Generation` to `SerialNumberGeneration`.\n- Derive `updateResourceName = \"invOrgParameters\"` from JSON_SCHEMA.\n- Leave `attValueToUpdate` missing if no value is provided.\n- success=false because a required param is still missing.\n\n### Example H (single OrganizationId recovered from chat history on first invocation)\nUSER_REQUEST:\n\"Update Serial number Generation to 1\"\nCHAT_HISTORY:\n\"USER: show org with OrganizationName INVT0GR01_INV11\nAI: - OrganizationId: 300100701340210; OrganizationCode: INVT0GR11; OrganizationName: INVT0GR01_INV11\"\nExpected behavior:\n- Recover the single OrganizationId `300100701340210` from CHAT_HISTORY.\n- Set `keyValues = [300100701340210]`.\n- Resolve `Serial number Generation` to `SerialNumberGeneration`.\n- Derive `updateResourceName = \"invOrgParameters\"`.\n- Set `attValueToUpdate = \"1\"`.\n- success=true when no other blocking issue exists."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"success\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"confidence_score\": {\n      \"type\": \"number\"\n    },\n    \"reasoning\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"feedback\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"missingRequiredParams\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"issues\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"type\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              \"message\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              }\n            },\n            \"required\": [\n              \"type\",\n              \"message\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        \"proposedClarifyingQuestions\": {\n          \"type\": \"array\",\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"missingRequiredParams\",\n        \"issues\",\n        \"proposedClarifyingQuestions\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"params\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"keyValues\": {},\n        \"updateResourceName\": {},\n        \"attNameToUpdate\": {},\n        \"attValueToUpdate\": {}\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"keyValues\",\n        \"updateResourceName\",\n        \"attNameToUpdate\",\n        \"attValueToUpdate\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"success\",\n    \"confidence_score\",\n    \"reasoning\",\n    \"feedback\",\n    \"params\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
