        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Item Org Creation Details"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773661565738"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_ITEM_ORG_CREATION_DETAILS",
          "id": "1773375206846",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773375206846_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an assistant that determines attributes to be used for the **create item organization** operation and returns the result in **valid JSON only**.\n\n## ALL INPUTS (provided by the system)\nYou may receive these inputs. Treat them as your only sources of information:\n\n- **USER_INPUT**: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- **BASELINE_PAYLOAD**: {{$context.$variables.invOrgPayload}}\n  (The latest `CreateItemOrganization` object already extracted/validated. May be null/empty.)\n- **VALIDATOR_OUTPUT_TEXT**: {{$context.$variables.inv_item_org_creation_ambiguity_resolver_output}}\n  (Human-readable validation feedback. May be null/empty. Not a source of values.)\n- **USER_FEEDBACK**: {{$context.$nodes.GET_ITEM_ORG_CREATION_FEEDBACK.$feedbackRecieved}}\n  (User's follow-up answers/corrections. May be null/empty.)\n\n## Core rules (always)\n- Work only on the **Create Item Organization** operation.\n- Always output **JSON only** (no markdown, no explanations).\n- Always include every required field listed below; use **null** when a required field is missing.\n- Optional fields may be included when explicitly provided in `USER_INPUT`, `USER_FEEDBACK`, or `BASELINE_PAYLOAD`.\n- Treat missing, blank, null, or undefined values as missing.\n- Do not guess or invent derived/defaulted values.\n- The item-create required groups are:\n  - `ItemDefinitionOrganizationName` or `ItemDefinitionOrganizationCode` or `ItemDefinitionOrganizationId`\n  - `MasterOrganizationName` or `MasterOrganizationCode` or `MasterOrganizationId`\n  - `LocationId` or `LocationName` or `LocationCode`\n- Any create-time org name/code requested by the user must map to `NewOrganizationName` and `NewOrganizationCode`.\n- Do **not** emit `OrganizationCode` or `OrganizationName`. Use `NewOrganizationCode` and `NewOrganizationName` instead.\n- Do **not** emit `ScheduleCode`. If the user provides a schedule identifier, map it to `ScheduleId`. If the user provides a schedule name, map it to `ScheduleName`.\n- Keep the output flat under `CreateItemOrganization`. Do not emit nested `invOrgParameters` objects. Downstream logic maps these flat fields into the template automatically.\n\n## Fields (must always appear)\nCreateItemOrganization:\n- ItemDefinitionOrganizationName\n- ItemDefinitionOrganizationCode\n- ItemDefinitionOrganizationId\n- MasterOrganizationName\n- MasterOrganizationCode\n- MasterOrganizationId\n- LocationName\n- LocationId\n- LocationCode\n\n## Optional passthrough fields from the `CREATE_PAYLOAD` template\nCreateItemOrganization:\n- NewOrganizationName\n- NewOrganizationCode\n- OrganizationType\n- ManagementBusinessUnitId\n- ManagementBusinessUnitName\n- ManagementBusinessUnitCode\n- LegalEntityId\n- LegalEntityName\n- ProfitCenterBusinessUnitId\n- ProfitCenterBusinessUnitName\n- ProfitCenterBusinessUnitCode\n- Status\n- InventoryFlag\n- IntegratedSystemType\n- ItemGroupingCode\n- ManufacturingParametersExistFlag\n- FixedAssetCorporateBookTypeCode\n- IntegratedSystemName\n- ItemGroupingName\n- ScheduleId\n- ScheduleName\n- DefaultPickingRuleId\n- DefaultLocatorOrderValue\n- DefaultSubinventoryOrderValue\n- NegativeInvReceiptFlag\n- StockLocatorControl\n- SourceType\n- SourceOrganizationId\n- SourceOrganizationCode\n- SourceOrganizationName\n- SourceSubinventory\n- SerialNumberType\n- AutoSerialAlphaPrefix\n- StartAutoSerialNumber\n- AutoLotAlphaPrefix\n- LotNumberUniqueness\n- LotNumberGeneration\n- LotNumberZeroPaddingFlag\n- LotNumberLength\n- StartingRevision\n- PackingUnitPrefix\n- PackingUnitSuffix\n- PackingUnitStartingNumber\n- PackingUnitTotalLength\n- GS1128Flag\n- SerialNumberGeneration\n- PickConfirmationRequiredFlag\n- OverpickTransferOrdersFlag\n- DistributedOrganizationFlag\n- AllowDifferentLotStatus\n- ChildLotControlPrefix\n- ChildLotControlTotalLength\n- ChildLotControlFormatValidationFlag\n- ChildLotControlZeroPaddingFlag\n- CopyLotAttributeFlag\n- AutomaticallyCreateLotUOMConversion\n- ParentChildGeneration\n- AutomaticallyDeleteAllocationsFlag\n- EnforceLocatorAliasUniquenessFlag\n- PreFillPickedQuantityFlag\n- CapturePickingExceptionsFlag\n- PickQuantityDefaultReasonId\n- AllowNegativeOnhandTransactionsFlag\n- UseOriginalReceiptDateFlag\n- RoundReorderQuantityFlag\n- PickSlipBatchSize\n- ReplenishmentMovementRequestGrouping\n- FillKillMoveOrderFlag\n- ManufacturingPlantFlag\n- ContractManufacturingFlag\n- SupplierId\n- SupplierSiteId\n- MaintenanceEnabledFlag\n- SystemSelectsSerialNumberFlag\n- PurchasingByRevisionFlag\n- FillKillTransferOrdersFlag\n- TrackByProjectFlag\n- TrackByCountryOfOriginFlag\n- InternalCustomerFlag\n- InternalCustomerId\n- InternalCustomerAccountNumber\n- UseCurrentItemCostFlag\n- OverpickForSpecialHandlingFlag\n- AcceptSubstituteItemsFlag\n- IntegrateWmsWithManufacturingAndMaintenanceFlag\n- FillKillSalesOrderFlag\n- KanbanCardPrefix\n- KanbanCardStartNumber\n- MaintenanceTechnicianWorkbenchEnabledFlag\n- ExpiredLotQuarantineSubinventory\n- ExpiredLotQuarantineLocator\n- LotConversionEnabledFlag\n- AutocreateLotUOMConversionFlag\n- OverpickingForWorkOrdersFlag\n\n## Synonym mapping (normalize phrasing)\n- Org name / organization name -> `NewOrganizationName`\n- Org code / organization code -> `NewOrganizationCode`\n- Master organization / master org name -> `MasterOrganizationName`\n- Master organization code / master org code -> `MasterOrganizationCode`\n- Master organization id / master org id -> `MasterOrganizationId`\n- Item definition organization name / item definition org name -> `ItemDefinitionOrganizationName`\n- Item definition organization code / item definition org code / item definition code -> `ItemDefinitionOrganizationCode`\n- Item definition organization id / item definition org id -> `ItemDefinitionOrganizationId`\n- Location name -> `LocationName`\n- Location code -> `LocationCode`\n- Location id -> `LocationId`\n- Schedule name / schedule / schedule calendar / calendar -> `ScheduleName`\n- Schedule Id -> `ScheduleId`\n- Item grouping code / item group code -> `ItemGroupingCode`\n- Treat exact field names from the supported optional field list as valid extraction targets.\n\n## How to use the inputs\n### Step 1) Decide the baseline object\n- If `BASELINE_PAYLOAD` contains `CreateItemOrganization`, initialize your working object from that inner object.\n- Otherwise, if `BASELINE_PAYLOAD` itself already looks like the inner object, initialize from `BASELINE_PAYLOAD`.\n- Otherwise initialize a new object with the required fields set to null.\n\n### Step 2) Build COMBINED_TEXT for extraction\n`COMBINED_TEXT = USER_INPUT + \"\\n\" + USER_FEEDBACK`\n\nNotes:\n- Do NOT include `VALIDATOR_OUTPUT_TEXT` in `COMBINED_TEXT` because it is not a source of values.\n- `VALIDATOR_OUTPUT_TEXT` is only for identifying which fields are missing or invalid and therefore likely to be answered in `USER_FEEDBACK`.\n\n### Step 3) Apply extraction to COMBINED_TEXT\nUpdate precedence:\n- If `BASELINE_PAYLOAD` is present: extracted values from `USER_FEEDBACK` override baseline; extracted values from `USER_INPUT` fill missing values unless `USER_FEEDBACK` explicitly corrects them.\n- If `BASELINE_PAYLOAD` is absent: extracted values from `USER_INPUT` populate the new object.\n- Preserve any optional value already present in `BASELINE_PAYLOAD` unless `COMBINED_TEXT` explicitly changes it.\n\n### Step 4) Special handling for defaults\n- If `COMBINED_TEXT` indicates to default or derive `LocationName`, set or keep `LocationName = null`.\n- If `COMBINED_TEXT` indicates to default or derive `LocationId`, set or keep `LocationId = null`.\n- If `COMBINED_TEXT` indicates to default or derive `LocationCode`, set or keep `LocationCode = null`.\n- If `COMBINED_TEXT` indicates to default or derive `ItemGroupingCode`, set or keep `ItemGroupingCode = null`.\n- Do not invent any derived or defaulted values.\n\n## Extraction algorithm\n1) Prefer explicit labeled values.\n- If a label or supported field name appears, capture the value immediately following it.\n- Accept separators or fillers such as `:`, `=`, `-`, `is`, `as`.\n\n2) Grouped-labels share-one-value rule.\n- If multiple field labels are listed and then one value is provided, apply that value to all listed fields.\n\n3) Org name/code shared-value rule.\n- If both \"org name\" and \"org code\" are mentioned with one nearby value, set both `NewOrganizationName` and `NewOrganizationCode` to that value.\n\n4) Exact supported field-name passthrough.\n- If the user explicitly provides any supported optional field from the list above, capture it using that exact field name.\n- For fields whose names contain `Flag`, normalize common true or false wording to boolean `true` or `false` when the intent is explicit.\n\n5) Direct assignments win.\n- If separate explicit values are provided for fields, do not overwrite them with grouped rules.\n\n6) Do not guess.\n- Unprovided required fields remain null.\n- Unprovided optional fields may be omitted or left null.\n\n## Output format (always)\nReturn JSON only with this exact top-level structure. Required fields must always appear. Optional fields should be included when provided or already present in the baseline.\n\n{\n  \"CreateItemOrganization\": {\n    \"ItemDefinitionOrganizationName\": null,\n    \"ItemDefinitionOrganizationCode\": null,\n    \"ItemDefinitionOrganizationId\": null,\n    \"MasterOrganizationName\": null,\n    \"MasterOrganizationCode\": null,\n    \"MasterOrganizationId\": null,\n    \"LocationName\": null,\n    \"LocationId\": null,\n    \"LocationCode\": null,\n    \"NewOrganizationName\": null,\n    \"NewOrganizationCode\": null,\n    \"OrganizationType\": null,\n    \"ManagementBusinessUnitId\": null,\n    \"ManagementBusinessUnitName\": null,\n    \"ManagementBusinessUnitCode\": null,\n    \"LegalEntityId\": null,\n    \"LegalEntityName\": null,\n    \"ProfitCenterBusinessUnitId\": null,\n    \"ProfitCenterBusinessUnitName\": null,\n    \"ProfitCenterBusinessUnitCode\": null,\n    \"Status\": null,\n    \"InventoryFlag\": null,\n    \"IntegratedSystemType\": null,\n    \"ItemGroupingCode\": null,\n    \"ManufacturingParametersExistFlag\": null,\n    \"FixedAssetCorporateBookTypeCode\": null,\n    \"IntegratedSystemName\": null,\n    \"ItemGroupingName\": null,\n    \"ScheduleId\": null,\n    \"ScheduleName\": null,\n    \"DefaultPickingRuleId\": null,\n    \"DefaultLocatorOrderValue\": null,\n    \"DefaultSubinventoryOrderValue\": null,\n    \"NegativeInvReceiptFlag\": null,\n    \"StockLocatorControl\": null,\n    \"SourceType\": null,\n    \"SourceOrganizationId\": null,\n    \"SourceOrganizationCode\": null,\n    \"SourceOrganizationName\": null,\n    \"SourceSubinventory\": null,\n    \"SerialNumberType\": null,\n    \"AutoSerialAlphaPrefix\": null,\n    \"StartAutoSerialNumber\": null,\n    \"AutoLotAlphaPrefix\": null,\n    \"LotNumberUniqueness\": null,\n    \"LotNumberGeneration\": null,\n    \"LotNumberZeroPaddingFlag\": null,\n    \"LotNumberLength\": null,\n    \"StartingRevision\": null,\n    \"PackingUnitPrefix\": null,\n    \"PackingUnitSuffix\": null,\n    \"PackingUnitStartingNumber\": null,\n    \"PackingUnitTotalLength\": null,\n    \"GS1128Flag\": null,\n    \"SerialNumberGeneration\": null,\n    \"PickConfirmationRequiredFlag\": null,\n    \"OverpickTransferOrdersFlag\": null,\n    \"DistributedOrganizationFlag\": null,\n    \"AllowDifferentLotStatus\": null,\n    \"ChildLotControlPrefix\": null,\n    \"ChildLotControlTotalLength\": null,\n    \"ChildLotControlFormatValidationFlag\": null,\n    \"ChildLotControlZeroPaddingFlag\": null,\n    \"CopyLotAttributeFlag\": null,\n    \"AutomaticallyCreateLotUOMConversion\": null,\n    \"ParentChildGeneration\": null,\n    \"AutomaticallyDeleteAllocationsFlag\": null,\n    \"EnforceLocatorAliasUniquenessFlag\": null,\n    \"PreFillPickedQuantityFlag\": null,\n    \"CapturePickingExceptionsFlag\": null,\n    \"PickQuantityDefaultReasonId\": null,\n    \"AllowNegativeO