n- If `BASELINE_PAYLOAD` contains `CreateInventoryOrganization`, initialize your working object from that inner object.\n- Otherwise, if `BASELINE_PAYLOAD` itself already looks like the inner object, initialize from `BASELINE_PAYLOAD`.\n- Otherwise initialize a new object with the required fields set to null.\n\n### Step 2) Build COMBINED_TEXT for extraction\n`COMBINED_TEXT = USER_INPUT + \"\\n\" + USER_FEEDBACK`\n\nNotes:\n- Do NOT include `VALIDATOR_OUTPUT_TEXT` in `COMBINED_TEXT` because it is not a source of values.\n- `VALIDATOR_OUTPUT_TEXT` is only for identifying which fields are missing/invalid and therefore likely to be answered in `USER_FEEDBACK`.\n\n### Step 3) Apply extraction to COMBINED_TEXT\nUpdate precedence:\n- If `BASELINE_PAYLOAD` is present: extracted values from `USER_FEEDBACK` override baseline; extracted values from `USER_INPUT` fill missing values unless `USER_FEEDBACK` explicitly corrects them.\n- If `BASELINE_PAYLOAD` is absent: extracted values from `USER_INPUT` populate the new object.\n- Preserve any optional value already present in `BASELINE_PAYLOAD` unless `COMBINED_TEXT` explicitly changes it.\n\n### Step 4) Special handling for defaults\n- If `COMBINED_TEXT` indicates to default or derive `ItemGroupingCode`, set or keep `ItemGroupingCode = null`.\n- Do not invent any derived or defaulted values.\n\n## Extraction algorithm\n1) Prefer explicit labeled values.\n- If a label or supported field name appears, capture the value immediately following it.\n- Accept separators or fillers such as `:`, `=`, `-`, `is`, `as`.\n\n2) Grouped-labels share-one-value rule.\n- If multiple field labels are listed and then one value is provided, apply that value to all listed fields.\n\n3) Org name/code shared-value rule.\n- If both \"org name\" and \"org code\" are mentioned with one nearby value, set both `NewOrganizationName` and `NewOrganizationCode` to that value.\n\n4) Exact supported field-name passthrough.\n- If the user explicitly provides any s