              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert assistant preparing the final user-facing validation summary for Inventory Organization creation.\n\nInputs\n1) Validation Result JSON:\n{{$context.$nodes.CHECK_INV_ORG_COPY_REQUIRED_ATTRIBUTES.$output.result}}\n\n2) Input Payload:\n{{$context.$variables.invOrgPayload}}\n\nInterpretation rules:\n- Treat `Validation Result JSON` as the only source of truth for required attribute validation.\n- Do not re-evaluate, re-check, or infer pass/fail for required attributes from the payload.\n- If the payload contains a `CreateCopyOrganization` object, use that inner object only for printing attribute values in section 3.\n- Otherwise use the payload object directly for printing attribute values in section 3.\n- If there is any mismatch between the payload and `Validation Result JSON`, trust `Validation Result JSON`.\n- Do not invent values and do not modify the payload.\n\nOutput requirements:\n- Do NOT output JSON.\n- Output must be concise, human readable, and in this exact structure:\n\n1) Overall Status: PASS or FAIL\n\n2) Missing/Invalid Required Attributes:\n- If `Validation Result JSON.missingAttributes` is empty: `None`\n- Else: bullet list in the same order as `Validation Result JSON.attributeResults`.\n- Include only the entries whose `status` is `FAIL`.\n- For `NewOrganizationName`, `NewOrganizationCode`, and `SourceOrganizationName`, use this format:\n  `<AttributeName> - <missing|null|blank>`\n- Use the `reason` value from the matching failed `attributeResults` entry.\n- For the location requirement when both are invalid, use this exact format:\n  `Location - missing all acceptable values (LocationName, LocationCode)`\n\n3) Attributes Summary:\n- If `Validation Result JSON.overallStatus` is `FAIL`: write `Not applicable (validation failed).`\n- If `Validation Result JSON.overallStatus` is `PASS`: list ALL of the following attributes one per line, in this order:\n  `NewOrganizationName`\n  `NewOrganizationCode`\n  `SourceOrganizationName`\n  `LocationCode`\n  `LocationName`\n- Use the format `<AttributeName>: <value>`.\n- If any listed attribute is null or missing, print `<AttributeName>: null`.\n\n4) Next Action for User:\n- If `Validation Result JSON.overallStatus` is `PASS`: `You can proceed with create inventory organization.`\n- If `Validation Result JSON.overallStatus` is `FAIL`: `Please provide values for the missing or invalid required attributes and resubmit.`\n\nKeep the tone professional and do not add any extra sections."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "CreateQueryFilter",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let result = { locationVal: { filterExpression: \"\" }, setup: { filterExpression: \"\"} };\n  // Access payload safely\n  const payload = $context.$nodes?.EXTRACT_SEARCH_DETAILS?.$output || {};\n\n  // Mapping user-friendly types to actual database fields\n  const typeToField = {\n    Country: \"CountryCode\",\n    City: \"TownOrCity\",\n    Zip: \"PostalCode\",\n    State: \"Region2\"\n  };\n\n  // Operator map to SQL-like operators\n  const operatorMap = {\n    EQUALS: \"=\",\n    NOT_EQUALS: \"!=\",\n    GREATER_THAN: \">\",\n    GREATER_THAN_EQUALS: \">=\",\n    LESS_THAN: \"<\",\n    LESS_THAN_EQUALS: \"<=\",\n    IN: \"IN\",\n    LIKE: \"LIKE\"\n  };\n\n  // Process extractedLocationDetails to build locationVal filter\n  const details = Array.isArray(payload.extractedLocationDetails) ? payload.extractedLocationDetails : [];\n  const fieldValues = {};\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < details.length; i++) {\n    const item = details[i] || {};\n    const field = typeToField[item.type];\n    if (!field) continue; // skip unknown types\n\n    const values = Array.isArray(item.values) ? item.values : [];\n    if (!fieldValues[field]) fieldValues[field] = new Set();\n\n    for (let j = 0; j < values.length; j++) {\n      const val = String(values[j]).trim();\n      if (val) fieldValues[field].add(val);\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Convert sets to arrays\n  const mappedValues = {};\n  for (const key in fieldValues) {\n    mappedValues[key] = Array.from(fieldValues[key]);\n  }\n // result.locationVal.mappedValues = mappedValues;\n\n  // Build locationVal filter expression\n  const locationValClauses = [];\n  const orderedFields = [\"TownOrCity\", \"CountryCode\", \"Region2\", \"PostalCode\"];\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < orderedFields.length; i++) {\n    const field = orderedFields[i];\n    const vals = mappedValues[field];\n    if (vals && vals.length) {\n      // Quote string values properly\n      const quotedVals = vals.map(v => \"'\" + String(v).replace(/'/g, \"''\") + \"'\");\n      locationValClauses.push(field + \" IN (\" + quotedVals.join(\",\") + \")\");\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (locationValClauses.length) {\n    // Append ActiveStatus filter\n    result.locationVal.filterExpression = locationValClauses.join(\" and \") + \" and ActiveStatus='A'\";\n  }\n\n  // Process matchedSetupAttribute to build setup filter\n  const attrs = Array.isArray(payload.matchedSetupAttribute) ? payload.matchedSetupAttribute : [];\n  const setupParts = [];\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < attrs.length; i++) {\n    const attr = attrs[i] || {};\n    const path = attr.path;\n    const rawOperator = String(attr.operator || \"\").toUpperCase();\n    const op = operatorMap[rawOperator] || rawOperator;\n    const values = Array.isArray(attr.values) ? attr.values : [];\n\n    if (path && op && values.length) {\n      let condition = \"\";\n      if (op === \"IN\") {\n        // Build IN clause\n        const inVals = values.map(v => {\n          if (typeof v === \"boolean\" || typeof v === \"number\") return String(v);\n          return \"'\" + String(v).replace(/'/g, \"''\") + \"'\";\n        });\n        condition = path + \" IN (\" + inVals.join(\",\") + \")\";\n      } else {\n        // Single value condition\n        const firstVal = values[0];\n        let valStr = \"\";\n        if (op === \"LIKE\") {\n          const escapedLikeValue = String(firstVal).trim().replace(/'/g, \"''\");\n          valStr = \"'%\" + escapedLikeValue + \"%'\";\n        } else if (typeof firstVal === \"boolean\" || typeof firstVal === \"number\") {\n          valStr = String(firstVal);\n        } else {\n          valStr = \"'\" + String(firstVal).replace(/'/g, \"''\") + \"'\";\n        }\n        condition = path + \" \" + op + \" \" + valStr;\n      }\n\n      setupParts.push(condition);\n\n      // Check if next valid condition exists for joinWithNext\n      if (i < attrs.length - 1) {\n        let nextValid = false;\n        for (let n = i + 1; n < attrs.length; n++) {\n          const nextAttr = attrs[n] || {};\n          if (nextAttr.path && Array.isArray(nextAttr.values) && nextAttr.values.length && nextAttr.operator) {\n            nextValid = true;\n            break;\n          }\n        }\n        if (nextValid) {\n          const join = String(attr.joinWithNext || \"AND\").toUpperCase() === \"OR\" ? \"or\" : \"and\";\n          setupParts.push(join);\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  result.setup.filterExpression = setupParts.join(\" \");\n\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776446000025"
          },
