              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are preparing the final user-facing summary for inventory plant parameter creation results.\n\nLOOP_RESULTS_JSON: {{$context.$nodes.FOR_EACH_PLANT_PARAMETER_ENTRY.$output}}\n\nInstructions:\n- Treat LOOP_RESULTS_JSON as the full result from all loop iterations.\n- It may contain an array of per-record results, or an object that contains that array.\n- Start with a clear summary of overall counts for passed and failed records.\n- Then provide a separate section that lists all records from the loop result.\n- Never show only a subset, sample, preview, or truncated selection of records.\n- A record is failed when Status is FAILED. Otherwise treat it as passed.\n- For every record, show OrganizationId, Status, FailureReason when present, and any other fields present in that record.\n- If OrganizationId is missing, show Unknown OrganizationId.\n- If a failure reason is missing for a failed record, show No failure reason returned.\n- Present the result in readable text, not raw JSON.\n- Do not invent details beyond LOOP_RESULTS_JSON."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Inventory Item Org Creation Ambiguity Resolver"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775432308230"
          },
          "code": "INVENTORY_ITEM_ORG_CREATION_AMBIGUITY_RESOLVER",
          "id": "1773662142527",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773662142527_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert assistant preparing the final user-facing validation summary for Item Organization creation.\n\nInputs\n1) Validation Result JSON:\n{{$context.$nodes.CHECK_ITEM_ORG_CREATION_REQUIRED_GROUPS.$output.result}}\n\n2) Input Payload:\n{{$context.$variables.invOrgPayload}}\n\nInterpretation rules:\n- Treat `Validation Result JSON` as the only source of truth for required attribute group validation.\n- Do not re-evaluate, re-check, or infer pass/fail for required groups from the payload.\n- If the payload contains a `CreateItemOrganization` object, use that inner object only for printing attribute values in section 3.\n- Otherwise use the payload object directly for printing attribute values in section 3.\n- If there is any mismatch between the payload and `Validation Result JSON`, trust `Validation Result JSON`.\n- Do not invent values and do not modify the payload.\n\nOutput requirements:\n- Do NOT output JSON.\n- Output must be concise, human readable, and in this exact structure:\n\n1) Overall Status: PASS or FAIL\n\n2) Missing/Invalid Required Attribute Groups:\n- If `Validation Result JSON.missingGroups` is empty: `None`\n- Else: bullet list in the same order as `Validation Result JSON.groupResults`.\n- Include only the groups whose `status` is `FAIL`.\n- Use this format for each failing group:\n  `<Group Label> - missing all acceptable values (<field1>, <field2>, ...)`\n- Use the `fields` list from the matching failed `groupResults` entry.\n\n3) Attributes Summary:\n- If `Validation Result JSON.overallStatus` is `FAIL`: write `Not applicable (validation failed).`\n- If `Validation Result JSON.overallStatus` is `PASS`: list ALL of the following attributes one per line, in this order:\n  `ItemDefinitionOrganizationName`\n  `ItemDefinitionOrganizationCode`\n  `ItemDefinitionOrganizationId`\n  `MasterOrganizationName`\n  `MasterOrganizationCode`\n  `MasterOrganizationId`\n  `LocationId`\n  `LocationCode`\n  `LocationName`\n  `NewOrganizationName`\n  `NewOrganizationCode`\n  `ItemGroupingCode`\n- Use the format `<AttributeName>: <value>`.\n- If any listed attribute is null or missing, print `<AttributeName>: null`.\n\n4) Next Action for User:\n- If `Validation Result JSON.overallStatus` is `PASS`: `You can proceed with create item organization.`\n- If `Validation Result JSON.overallStatus` is `FAIL`: `Please provide at least one value for each failing required group and resubmit.`\n\nKeep the tone professional and do not add any extra sections."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Inventory Org Creation Ambiguity Resolver"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775432312392"
