          "id": "1776444000005",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776444000005_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are preparing the final user-facing summary for the business function result of query inventory setup with location filter.\n\nBUSINESS_FUNCTION_OUTPUT_JSON: {{$context.$nodes.QUERY_INVENTORY_SETUP_WITH_LOCATION.$output}}\nSETUP_FILTER_ATTRIBUTES_JSON: {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SEARCH_DETAILS.$output.matchedSetupAttribute}}\nLOCATION_FILTER_ATTRIBUTES_JSON: {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_SEARCH_DETAILS.$output.extractedLocationDetails}}\n\nInstructions:\n- Treat BUSINESS_FUNCTION_OUTPUT_JSON as the complete business function output.\n- Treat SETUP_FILTER_ATTRIBUTES_JSON only as the filter query input that was used for the InventoryOrganization API call.\n- Treat LOCATION_FILTER_ATTRIBUTES_JSON as the source of the LocationFilter value to display in the final response when location filters exist.\n- Present the result in readable text, not raw JSON.\n- Never invent details beyond BUSINESS_FUNCTION_OUTPUT_JSON, SETUP_FILTER_ATTRIBUTES_JSON, and LOCATION_FILTER_ATTRIBUTES_JSON.\n- Do not show a separate filter criteria section.\n- Do not show SQL-like expressions, operators, join conditions, or dynamic filter text.\n- If LOCATION_FILTER_ATTRIBUTES_JSON is present, show a single field named LocationFilter for each returned record. Build LocationFilter from LOCATION_FILTER_ATTRIBUTES_JSON only, using the extracted location type/value pairs in readable text. Do not show LocationId.\n- If the response indicates failure, partial success, or no records, explain that clearly using only details present in BUSINESS_FUNCTION_OUTPUT_JSON.\n- Never show only a subset, sample, preview, or truncated selection of returned records.\n- When records are present, include every returned record.\n- Display returned records using bullet points.\n- Each returned record must be a separate bullet point.\n- For each record, show only these fields in this order when present: OrganizationId, OrganizationCode, LocationFilter, OrganizationName, then each attribute from SETUP_FILTER_ATTRIBUTES_JSON with the value taken from SETUP_FILTER_ATTRIBUTES_JSON.\n- While showing filter attributes, use SETUP_FILTER_ATTRIBUTES_JSON as the source of truth for the values. Do not extract those attribute values from BUSINESS_FUNCTION_OUTPUT_JSON.\n- If an attribute name is LocationId, do not show it.\n- If SETUP_FILTER_ATTRIBUTES_JSON is empty or unavailable, show only OrganizationId, OrganizationCode, optional LocationFilter, and OrganizationName for each returned record.\n- Do not show any additional fields from BUSINESS_FUNCTION_OUTPUT_JSON beyond OrganizationId, OrganizationCode, and OrganizationName.\n- Keep the summary concise and minimal.\n\nExample expected shape:\n- OrganizationId: 300100123456789; OrganizationCode: ZDQ1; LocationFilter: Country=US, State=CA; OrganizationName: ZDQ1; ManufacturingPlantFlag: true"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
